# Run these commands from the REPOSITORY ROOT:
#   cp .env.dist .env
#   cargo tauri signer generate
#
# Both dotenv files belong at the repository root.
# Choose a password when prompted. Back up the private key and password securely.
# .env is ignored by Git. Agents must NEVER read it.
#
# Set all three environment variables below using the generated key contents.
# Paste the entire single-line key values printed by the signer.
# Required by native builds, including cargo tauri dev/build, tests and Clippy.
TAURI_SIGNING_PUBLIC_KEY=<key>
TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=<key>
TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD='<password>'
# Use an explicitly empty password only for an unencrypted private key.
#
# Native commands:
#   cargo tauri dev
#   cargo tauri build
# Rust loads the root .env at build time; existing environment variables win.
#
# Set TAURI_SIGNING_PUBLIC_KEY in .github/workflows/publish.yml to the matching
# public key value. Add these GitHub Actions repository secrets:
#   TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY: generated private key value
#   TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD: password chosen above
# An unencrypted key uses an empty password secret.
# CI supplies all three environment variables directly to cargo tauri build.
# See docs/UPDATES.md for the release flow and planned in-app controls.
